From 9a7a5865d6ebdeac1ac63c6957cf3b4efdc0edbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:35:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp2: imx415: Add the temporal noise reduction
 calibration

Enable the temporal noise reduction with the MFNR calibration of the
Rockchip IQ file for this sensor (normal mode, LSNR setting), converted
with mfnr-iq2yaml.py.

The IQ weight limits are close to zero, as the vendor pairs them with
its closed motion detection. Without it, low-contrast motion fades over
about ten frames. The limits are set to 64 up to ISO 200, 96 at ISO 400
and 128 from ISO 800, which keeps a moving object's trail within about
three frames in the dark at the cost of weaker averaging there.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
